-ESANet uses \(640\times448\) inputs, batch size 8, SGD with learning
-rate 0.01, momentum 0.9, weight decay \(10^{-4}\) and a OneCycle
-learning-rate schedule. Class weights account for the imbalance between
-obstacle and background pixels using the authors' median-frequency
-method. We train for 500 epochs, following the published training
-duration, and select the checkpoint with the best validation obstacle
-IoU. Learning curves are checked for convergence before comparing input
-types.
